     <target value="40"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Distribution grid extended and additional households connected by the government 
Indicator: 1,050 new customers in Espiritu Santo and Malekula connected by 2025 to reduce women&amp;apos;s time poverty, with subsidized connections for 100 households headed by women 
Progress/Status: The Department of Energy is undertaking consultations with the utilities in Malekula and Espiritu Santo to facilitate an additional 1,050 household connections.

No timeline for the achievement of the required number of household connections has been presented by the government yet. 
Data Source: Annual corporate report by utility concession holders 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2017"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2025-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="1050"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3  Indicator 2</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Distribution grid extended and additional households connected by the government 
Indicator: 21 km transmission line and 79 km distribution line constructed on Espiritu Santo and Malekula by 2025 
Progress/Status: Of a total of 100km of grid infrastructure, 40.5km transmission and distribution lines were commissioned in Malekula in October 2023, while 45km of transmission lines in Espiritu Santo were commissioned in August 2024.

Low Voltage reticulation systems:
Malekula: The transmission lines in Malekula were commissioned in Q4 2023. Funding has been allocated for the design and construction of the LV reticulation systems. A Project Management Consultant has been recruited in Q1 2025, who will support the LV infrastructure implementation, including detailed design and procurement. The tender and procurement process is envisaged to be completed by Q2 2026.  

Espiritu Santo: A budget application for the LV reticulation systems in Espiritu Santo still has to be submitted. The timeline for design work and construction of Lot 2 LV infrastructure will be confirmed as soon as the budget has been approved. 
Data Source: Annual corporate report by utility concession holders 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2017"></baseline>
    <period>
